ReadMe

Drill ID: JD_2026_08_W2_DeepSpaceTransmissionControl

Class Name: DeepSpaceTransmissionControl

Difficulty: Level 4 — Creative OOP Challenge

Estimated Time: 100–140 minutes

Actual Time Taken: 154 minutes

Written by: Chanwoo Park

Problem
Build a deep-space transmission control system that schedules different
transmission types to capacity-limited ground stations.

Program Flow
- Create Mission Control.
- Register stations and multiple transmission subtypes.
- Schedule and execute transmissions.
- Handle invalid operations through custom exceptions.
- Release station capacity when transmissions complete.
- Archive transmissions.
- Safely batch-remove archived transmissions from active operations.
- Print operational reports.
- Save archived transmission records to a file.

Class Responsibilities
- MissionControlApp: Console layer and exception handling.
- Transmission: Owns common transmission data and lifecycle rules.
- ImageTransmission / TelemetryTransmission: Provide subtype-specific load behavior.
- GroundStation: Owns station capacity and current assignments.
- MissionControl: Coordinates object collaboration and collections.
- TransmissionLogWriter: Persists archived records.
- InvalidTransmissionOperationException: Represents invalid business operations.

Requirements
- Protect state transitions inside Transmission.
- Use polymorphism for communication-load calculation.
- Keep Transmission and GroundStation state consistent.
- Do not expose mutable internal collections.
- Safely remove archived transmissions during batch cleanup.
- Propagate business exceptions to this application layer.

Learning Objective
Practice Level 4 object ownership, polymorphism, collection encapsulation,
safe iteration/removal, multi-object consistency, exception propagation,
and file persistence.